":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in v4.5-beta1\nNot reproducible in v4.5-dev5\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.beta1 - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1650 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6636) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-10300H CPU @ 2.50GHz (8 threads) - 39.82 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nI am profiling a project with ~ 1500 dynamically created collision objects (the creation is not per-frame, but some old collision geometry is deleted and some new collision geometry is created every couple of seconds in my test case).  I am testing using raycasts in conjunction with our custom projectile ballistics code, with a target maximum of 2048 projectiles active at a time.\n\nIn the latest v4.5-Beta1, when testing with the Jolt 3D Physics engine, I noticed that the raycast times continued to increase.  See the Output window in the following screenshot of the MRP:\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/560f0d50-afe0-4d36-9cec-a1dc5920f23c)\n\nHere is the (expected) behavior on the v4.5-dev5:\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4ce8132f-0a2d-4dd4-b972-f166e63b7677)\n\nThe execution time seems to grow linearly.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nThe code runs as a tool in the MRP (attached below).  The collision objects are generated dynamically, and then a bunch of raycasts are timed.  Switch to the 3D preview (and scroll out a little), then make sure the Output window is visible.  Every 5 seconds or so the average raycast execution time is printed in the Output.  Notice that in the v4.5-Beta1 the execution time keeps increasing, but in v4.5-dev5 it hovers around a lower value (about 3 us / raycast, on my machine).\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[slow-raycast-jolt-MRP.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20890246/slow-raycast-jolt-MRP.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107951/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107951/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}